    <h2>If You Have Two Nights</h2>

    <p>
      Let Évora have one substantial portion of the trip.
    </p>

    <p>
      Then allow the additional time to begin introducing you to the Alentejo
      beyond the walls.
    </p>

    <p>
      That doesn't mean trying to cover the entire region.
    </p>

    <p>Quite the opposite.</p>

    <p>
      The Alentejo is too large and too varied to become another checklist.
    </p>

    <p>
      The additional time simply allows you to begin understanding the
      relationship between Évora and the landscape surrounding it.
    </p>

    <h2>A Simple Way to Decide</h2>

    <p>Ask yourself one question:</p>

    <blockquote>
      <p><strong>What role do I want Évora to play in this trip?</strong></p>
    </blockquote>

    <p>If the answer is:</p>

    <p>
      <strong>
        “I want to see an important historic Portuguese city while staying in
        Lisbon.”
      </strong>
    </p>

    <p>Choose the <strong>day trip</strong>.</p>

    <p>If the answer is:</p>

    <p>
      <strong>
        “I want Évora itself to feel like one of the places I visited in
        Portugal.”
      </strong>
    </p>

    <p>Choose <strong>one night</strong>.</p>

    <p>If the answer is:</p>

    <p>
      <strong>“I want Évora to introduce me to the Alentejo.”</strong>
    </p>

    <p>Choose <strong>two nights</strong>.</p>

    <p>There isn't a universally correct answer.</p>

    <p>
      There is a trip that fits what you actually want to experience.
    </p>

    <h2>The Bottom Line</h2>

    <p>
      Évora does not require an overnight simply because it is important.
    </p>

    <p>
      A well-planned day trip can give you a meaningful introduction to the
      city.
    </p>

    <p>But staying changes what the visit becomes.</p>

    <p>One night creates room for Évora itself.</p>

    <p>A second begins creating room for the Alentejo.</p>

    <p>
      So instead of asking whether Évora is “worth” staying overnight, ask:
    </p>

    <blockquote>
      <p><strong>How much of Évora do I want the trip to become?</strong></p>
    </blockquote>

    <p>Then give it the time that answer deserves.</p>

    <blockquote>
      <p>
        <strong>
          A day trip lets you see Évora. An overnight lets you experience
          Évora. A second night begins to open the Alentejo.
        </strong>
      </p>
    </blockquote>

